{
  "version": 18,
  "variables": [
    {
      "key": "dag_id",
      "type": "query",
      "input": "timeseries by:{dag_id}, x=count(airflow.ti.start) | fields dag_id | limit 500",
      "visible": true,
      "editable": true,
      "multiple": true
    },
    {
      "key": "task_id",
      "type": "query",
      "input": "timeseries by:{task_id}, x=count(airflow.ti.start) | fields task_id | limit 500",
      "visible": true,
      "editable": true,
      "multiple": true
    },
    {
      "key": "pool_name",
      "type": "query",
      "input": "timeseries by:{pool_name}, x=avg(airflow.pool.open_slots) | fields pool_name | limit 200",
      "visible": true,
      "editable": true,
      "multiple": true
    },
    {
      "key": "executor_class_name",
      "type": "query",
      "input": "timeseries by:{executor_class_name}, x=avg(airflow.executor.running_tasks) | fields executor_class_name | limit 50",
      "visible": true,
      "editable": true,
      "multiple": true
    },
    {
      "key": "worker_name",
      "type": "query",
      "input": "timeseries by:{worker_name}, x=avg(airflow.edge_worker.status) | fields worker_name | limit 200",
      "visible": true,
      "editable": true,
      "multiple": true
    },
    {
      "key": "hostname",
      "type": "query",
      "input": "timeseries by:{hostname}, x=count(airflow.scheduler_heartbeat) | fields hostname | limit 200",
      "visible": true,
      "editable": true,
      "multiple": true
    }
  ],
  "tiles": {
    "0": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "",
      "content": "# Airflow Fleet Metrics \u2014 Dynatrace Dashboard\n\nEnvironment: Airflow 3.x, OTLP metrics+traces on (`otel_prefix=\"airflow\"`), hybrid **CeleryExecutor + KubernetesExecutor**, **Edge workers** in use, **OpenLineage** enabled, ~200+ DAGs / high concurrency (large scale). Built with DQL tiles (Grail). Metrics never carry `run_id` \u2014 only traces do; no tile here filters a metric by `run_id`.\n\n**Cardinality note:** at this scale, `dag_id` and `dag_id \u00d7 task_id` splits are capped/top-N by default and expect the `dag_id`/`task_id` dashboard variables to be used to scope the view \u2014 see per-tile notes in Sections 4 and 5.",
      "bounds": {
        "top": 0,
        "left": 0,
        "width": 1520,
        "height": 110
      }
    },
    "1": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "",
      "content": "## 1. Cluster Health / Heartbeats",
      "bounds": {
        "top": 114,
        "left": 0,
        "width": 1520,
        "height": 40
      }
    },
    "2": {
      "type": "data",
      "title": "Scheduler / DAG Processor / Triggerer heartbeat rate",
      "query": "timeseries scheduler=count(airflow.scheduler_heartbeat), dag_processor=count(airflow.dag_processor_heartbeat), triggerer=count(airflow.triggerer_heartbeat), by:{hostname}, interval:1m",
      "visualization": "lineChart",
      "visualizationSettings": {},
      "bounds": {
        "top": 158,
        "left": 0,
        "width": 756,
        "height": 304
      },
      "subtitle": "Absence detection: a flat 0 line for any series for >N minutes means that component stopped heartbeating."
    },
    "3": {
      "type": "data",
      "title": "Scheduler heartbeats in last 5 min",
      "query": "timeseries value=sum(airflow.scheduler_heartbeat), by:{hostname}, from:-5m",
      "visualization": "singleValue",
      "visualizationSettings": {
        "thresholds": [
          {
            "field": "value",
            "rules": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "comparator": "<=",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "comparator": ">",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "bounds": {
        "top": 158,
        "left": 760,
        "width": 376,
        "height": 304
      },
      "subtitle": "Alert-worthy: red if zero scheduler heartbeats in the last 5 min (tune window to your heartbeat interval). Rebuilt as a `timeseries` count-in-window check (this tenant doesn't use `fetch metrics`); a raw \"minutes since last heartbeat\" value isn't directly expressible via `timeseries`, which reports aggregated buckets rather than the underlying data-point timestamps."
    },
    "4": {
      "type": "data",
      "title": "Triggerer heartbeats in last 5 min",
      "query": "timeseries value=sum(airflow.triggerer_heartbeat), by:{hostname}, from:-5m",
      "visualization": "singleValue",
      "visualizationSettings": {
        "thresholds": [
          {
            "field": "value",
            "rules": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "comparator": "<=",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "comparator": ">",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "bounds": {
        "top": 158,
        "left": 1140,
        "width": 376,
        "height": 304
      },
      "subtitle": "Alert-worthy: red if zero triggerer heartbeats in the last 5 min (tune window to your heartbeat interval). Rebuilt as a `timeseries` count-in-window check (this tenant doesn't use `fetch metrics`)."
    },
    "5": {
      "type": "data",
      "title": "Per-job start / end / heartbeat_failure",
      "query": "timeseries schedulerStart=sum(airflow.scheduler_job_start), schedulerEnd=sum(airflow.scheduler_job_end), schedulerHbFail=sum(airflow.scheduler_heartbeat_failure), triggererStart=sum(airflow.triggerer_job_start), triggererEnd=sum(airflow.triggerer_job_end), triggererHbFail=sum(airflow.triggerer_heartbeat_failure)",
      "visualization": "lineChart",
      "visualizationSettings": {},
      "bounds": {
        "top": 466,
        "left": 0,
        "width": 1136,
        "height": 304
      },
      "subtitle": "REVIEW: {job_name}_start/_end/_heartbeat_failure bakes the job type into the metric name (scheduler_*, triggerer_*), it is not a queryable dimension \u2014 confirm the full set of job_name values your deployment emits (e.g. DagProcessorJob) against the metrics doc before relying on this tile."
    },
    "6": {
      "type": "data",
      "title": "Task instances killed for missing heartbeats",
      "query": "timeseries value=sum(airflow.task_instances_without_heartbeats_killed), by:{dag_id}",
      "visualization": "lineChart",
      "visualizationSettings": {
        "thresholds": [
          {
            "field": "value",
            "rules": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "comparator": ">",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "bounds": {
        "top": 466,
        "left": 1140,
        "width": 376,
        "height": 304
      },
      "subtitle": "Alert-worthy: any nonzero value indicates zombie task cleanup."
    },
